      "title": "Half-turn and quarter-turn cardinality obstructions",
      "summary": "An odd-cardinality no-three-in-line set invariant under a half-turn has at most one point, so a 153-point set cannot have half-turn symmetry. A quarter-turn-invariant no-three-in-line set has cardinality divisible by four or equal to one, excluding quarter-turn symmetry at cardinalities 153 and 154.",
